In the following chapter the wind tunnel experiments, that guided the set up of the numerical simulations, are presented. First, in Section 3.1, the selected wind tunnel is presented, while in Section 3.2 the test model is described. Finally the measurement techniques and the test parameters are described respectively in Section 3.3 and Section 3.4.
3.1 Wind Tunnel Facility
The S. De Ponte wind tunnel of Politecnico di Milano is a closed circuit wind tunnel equipped with a closed aeronautical test chamber which has dimensions of 1.5m x 1m x 3m. Thanks to some devices like turning vanes, honeycomb rectifier grids and screens, the maximum achievable speed in the test chamber is 55m/s with a turbulence level lower than 0.1%. The advantage of using such wind tunnel is that it ensures proper distances of the propellers from the chamber walls, thus reducing possible mutual interactional effects, but it also guaranties low costs of the tests. A technical drawing of the facility together with its dimensions are shown in Figure 3.1.
Figure 3.1: Technical drawing of the De Ponte wind tunnel.
