A lifting line element is a 1-D model of a thin slender lifting bodies, thus it can be successfully adopted to model bodies with high aspect ratios like wings or blades. The method intrinsecally considers the viscous effects, since it is based on tabulated and precomputed values of lift, drag and moment two-dimensional sectional coefficient as function of the local Reynolds number, Mach number and angle of attack.
