6.2 Preliminary Variopropeller Numerical Simulations
The main objective of this work is the analysis of rotor interactions for an eVTOL. Thus the simulations have been performed in such configurations that correctly represent and reproduce these particular vehicles, in both flight conditions and propeller layouts. Since eVTOLs, for example the Vahana aircraft, are designed to flight over populated areas and for a limited range, their cruise speed is typically around 100 km/h (i.e. 28 m/s). As a result, the Mach number measured at the blade tip on the real vehicle, reaches the value of 0.5. Since the geometry of the rotor is fixed , which is the same selected also for wind tunnel tests, the conservation of compressibility flow similarity at the model blade tip imposes a rotational speed of the rotor in the simulations of 7000 RPM. The Reynolds number based on the propeller disk diameter and on the rotational velocity evaluated at 70%R results to be equal to ReD = 1.93e6. The propeller model has a internal mechanical system which permits to change the collective blade pitch, that consequently induces different performances of the propeller. In the following simulations, the blade pitch measured at 75% of the rotor radius is set to θ = 25.5◦, since this value guarantees the maximum efficiency for an advance ratio of J = 0.8 (calculated according to 5.6). This choice is dictated by the fact that such advance ratio corresponds to a free stream velocity of 100 km/h (28 m/s) that is considered as a eVTOL cruise flight, and operating at maximum propeller efficiency guaranties lower consumed electrical power and thus further range of flight. To set reference conditions for the comparison of propeller interaction results, a series of tests are performed considering the same pitch angle, θ = 25.5◦, but varying the advance ratio between 0.1 and 1. The DUST simulation parameters are the optimum one found for the APC blade: 10 revolutions with 72 time instants each, and 41 lifting line elements in span. The nacelle is computed with